# Single source of truth for the GraalVM that compiles `vis-python-worker`.
#
# GraalVM COMMUNITY Edition, the newest release: this image is a few hundred
# classes around one native bridge, so the memory ceiling that keeps vis' own
# binary on an older train (its points-to analysis does not converge on that
# tree) does not apply here, and the two repos pin independently. CE, never
# Oracle GraalVM: only CE's Classpath Exception keeps the shipped executable
# FOSS. GRAAL_MAX_VERSION exists so a half-bumped pin fails before a release
# job spends an hour on it; a deliberate lift moves every key, tag and digest
# together and is proven by a green `clojure -T:build worker-image` first.
#
# Read by .github/actions/setup-graalvm-25 (shell) and build.clj (regex) —
# keep it plain KEY="value". There is NO macos-x64 (Intel) community build:
# `worker-platforms` in build.clj excludes darwin-x64 for that reason.

GRAAL_EDITION="GraalVM CE"
GRAAL_VERSION="25.3.4.1"
GRAAL_PIN_LOCKED="true"
GRAAL_MAX_VERSION="25.3.4.1"
GRAAL_TAG="graal-25.3.4.1"
GRAAL_ASSET_VERSION="25i3-25.0.4.1"
GRAAL_VENDOR_VERSION="GraalVM CE 25.3.4.1+1.1"
